## 2. IS 2062 E250, quickly, just so I have something to compare against

*(Going off memory and past project experience here — should double check against whatever the current revision says if I ever need exact numbers for a real calc.)*

* **Yield strength:** 250 MPa min (drops a bit for thicker sections)
* **Tensile strength:** 410 MPa min
* **Elongation:** roughly 23% min
* **Composition:** Carbon around 0.22% max, Mn up to 1.5%, S & P capped around 0.045% each — depends on which quality grade (A/B/C/BR)
* **Heat treatment / Toughness:** No mandatory normalizing, no toughness pathway of its own — it's just a good general structural grade

