## 3. What A516 Grade 70 actually says

Pulling this straight from the A516/A516M-04 document rather than trusting memory.

### Grades come as strength bands, not single numbers

| Grade | Tensile (ksi/MPa) | Yield min (ksi/MPa) | Elong. in 8 in [200mm] min % | Elong. in 2 in [50mm] min % |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **55 [380]** | 55–75 [380–515] | 30 [205] | 23 | 27 |
| **60 [415]** | 60–80 [415–550] | 32 [220] | 21 | 25 |
| **65 [450]** | 65–85 [450–585] | 35 [240] | 19 | 23 |
| **70 [485]** | **70–90 [485–620]** | **38 [260]** | **17** | **21** |

> **Note on Elongation:** Two elongation columns tripped me up for a second — it's not a contradiction, ASTM just reports elongation against two different gauge lengths depending on what the order specifies. A "17%" and a "21%" can both be correct for the same plate.

### Chemistry for Grade 70 (up to 1/2 in [12.5 mm] thick)
* **Carbon:** max 0.27% (climbs to 0.31% once you're past 8 in — thicker section cools slower, so the chemistry has to compensate)
* **Manganese:** 0.85–1.20%
* **Phosphorus & Sulfur:** both capped at 0.035%
* **Silicon:** 0.15–0.40%

### Heat treatment (Section 5) — the part that actually matters here
* **Up to 1.50 in [40 mm]:** As-rolled by default, can be ordered normalized or stress relieved.
* **Over 1.50 in [40 mm]:** Must be normalized. No way around it.
* **Impact-tested plate:** If Charpy testing gets invoked on anything 1.5 in or under, it gets normalized too, unless the design specifically says otherwise.

### Supplementary requirements worth knowing about
* **S5:** Charpy V-Notch Impact Test — the core requirement that proves the toughness promised by the scope statement.
* **S1:** Vacuum treatment.
* **S8 / S11 / S12:** Ultrasonic examination, depending on method (A435 straight-beam, A577 angle-beam, A578 for special/clad plate).
* **S9:** Magnetic particle examination.

> Plain A516 with nothing else called out is a fairly ordinary plate. The toughness story only really kicks in once S5 gets pulled in, and normalizing along with it.

